## 4.0a The worked example (one SELL decision, one trade, one null draw)
**The decision.** Decision j = 181, 2022-06-17 (the last session of its week). Master SIGN rows: Nifty 100 SELL (2022-06-17), Midcap 100 SELL (2022-06-17), Smallcap 100 SELL (2022-06-17); not all three BUY, so the regime is SELL.
The basket in force (effective 2022-06-16) has n = 8 stocks. Indicator I1 (close > 50-day EMA) on their closes up to 2022-06-17:

| stock | basket weight | close | ema50 | EMA50 test: close > EMA50 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| SIYSIL.NS | 0.1250 | 502.09 | 523.45 | drop |
| GHCL.NS | 0.1250 | 549.36 | 559.94 | drop |
| VTL.NS | 0.1250 | 255.75 | 341.54 | drop |
| OIL.NS | 0.1250 | 169.77 | 164.83 | keep |
| HINDALCO.NS | 0.1250 | 333.70 | 435.79 | drop |
| NATIONALUM.NS | 0.1250 | 75.70 | 97.54 | drop |
| RKFORGE.NS | 0.1250 | 156.05 | 167.20 | drop |
| HGINFRA.NS | 0.1250 | 555.70 | 573.25 | drop |

k = 1 kept, with basket weights adding to 0.1250; the other 0.8750 of the book goes to the sleeve, half GOLDBEES and half LBES cash (0.4375 each).
**The trade** (next session, 2022-06-20, at each instrument's OHLC4): portfolio value before V = 1.995009; value traded = 0.959202; cost = traded x 20.8 / 2 / 10,000 = 0.000998; every target is then scaled by (V - cost) / V = 0.999500. Kept after the trade: OIL.NS. NAV at that day's close 1.983437.
**The path.** I1 at 20.8 bps: NAV 1.0000 on 2019-01-02 -> 3.9523 on 2026-11-04; 1,935 sessions, years = (1,935 - 1) / 252 = 7.675; CAGR = 3.9523^(1/7.675) - 1 = 19.61%.
**One null draw** (I1, draw_id 0, seed `default_rng([4, 1, 0])`, u of shape (411, 197)): on the same decision the draw keeps the k = 1 stocks of the 8 with the smallest u: SIYSIL.NS (the indicator kept OIL.NS). Everything else is as the strategy. That draw's after-cost CAGR is 20.78%.

